    {
      "day": 21,
      "line": "🐪 A trader from the downriver village walks into Haven, pack heavy, smile practiced. River-mud on their boots, river-gossip on their tongue."
    },
    {
      "day": 22,
      "line": "A cart-driver with flour on their sleeves waits a while, then moves on down the road. Word travels about that, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 51,
      "line": "🧳 Word of Haven’s the televised games, new bindings is doing work out there — Word comes late, through traders: The Red Table and Emberhold have bound together — The Red Table primary. Other fires are climbing, too."
    },
    {
      "day": 63,
      "line": "🧳 Word comes late, through traders: Thornfield has bound itself to The Red Table. The region's map is being redrawn — not by Haven."
    },
    {
      "day": 64,
      "line": "🧳 A trader lingers after the meal — your fire eats well, and word travels with full bellies. \"East, past the river — three fires walk as ONE now. They've got a speaker for SPEAKERS. Thought you should know there's bigger games than yours.\""
    },
